    "readout_text": "The probability that Flora will eventually land on 10 is \\boxed{\\dfrac{1}{2}}. Therefore, m + n = 1 + 2 = 3.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Define P(n):** Let P(n) be the probability that Flora eventually lands on position n.\n\n2. **Base Case:** P(0) = 1 since Flora starts at 0.\n\n3. **Recursive Relation:** For any n ≥ 1,\n   \\[\n   P(n) = \\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} P(k) \\cdot \\frac{1}{2^{n - k}}\n   \\]\n   This is because to reach n, Flora must have been at some position k < n and then jumped exactly (n - k) units.\n\n4. **Calculate Initial Values:**\n   - P(1) = P(0) * (1/2) = 1/2\n   - P(2) = P(0)*(1/4) + P(1)*(1/2) = 1/4 + 1/4 = 1/2\n   - P(3) = P(0)*(1/8) + P(1)*(1/4) + P(2)*(1/2) = 1/8 + 1/8 + 1/4 = 1/2\n   - Similarly, P(4) = 1/2, and this pattern continues for all n ≥ 1.\n\n5. **Conclusion:** For any n ≥ 1, P(n) = 1/2. Therefore, P(10) = 1/2.\n\n6. **Simplify and Compute m + n:** The probability is 1/2, so m = 1 and n = 2. Thus, m + n = 3.\n\n\\boxed{3}",
